$$\text{Rate of salt in} = C_{in}(t) \times R_{in} = \frac{1}{4}\left(1+\frac{1}{2} \sin t\right) \times 2 = \frac{1}{2}\left(1+\frac{1}{2} \sin t\right) = \frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{4} \sin t \text{ oz/min}.$$

**2. Rate of salt out:**
The concentration of salt in the tank at time $t$ is $C_{out}(t) = \frac{S(t)}{V} = \frac{S(t)}{100} \text{ oz/gal}$.
The outflow rate is $R_{out} = 2 \text{ gal/min}$.
$$\text{Rate of salt out} = C_{out}(t) \times R_{out} = \frac{S(t)}{100} \times 2 = \frac{S(t)}{50} \text{ oz/min}.$$

